// Placed blocks resting on loose ground (sand, rubble) are carried by it: a pillar stub and a
// ledge built on a sand floor stay rigid instead of crumbling into powder and rolling away.
map
################################
################################
#..............................#
#..............................#
#..............................#
#..............................#
#..............................#
#...............@..............#
#ssssssssssssssssssssssssssssss#
#ssssssssssssssssssssssssssssss#
################################
end
give WoodPillar 20
give Brick 20
place 2 6 0 WoodPillar
place 3 6 -1 WoodPillar
place 4 6 -2 WoodPillar
place 5 6 -3 WoodPillar
// a short ledge off the stub's top
place 6 7 -3 WoodPillar
place 7 8 -3 WoodPillar
// a brick stub on the sand to the left
place 8 -5 0 Brick
place 9 -5 -1 Brick
expect 20 static:WoodBeam == 6
expect 600 static:WoodBeam == 6
expect 600 static:StoneBrick == 2
expect 600 is:8,-3,WoodBeam == 1
expect 600 count:Sand == 60
